    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0177" n="43" xml:id="pg43"/>

                <head>No. 37.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tree
                        to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States.</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 30, 1888</date>.
                        (Received July 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 359.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: As the money coined and put in circulation
                    by a new state has, perhaps, a certain interest, I have ventured to send you
                    to-day by post, under a separate cover, specimens of the first moneys ever
                    coined by the Independent State of the Congo.</p>
                <p>The package contains specimens of pieces of a half franc, and of 1, 2, and 5
                    francs in silver, and of 1, 2, 5, and 10 centimes in copper. No gold pieces have
                    been coined as yet.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lambert
                        Tree.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
